      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Erythema in darker-skinned patients can be more challenging to detect due to the natural pigmentation of the skin. However, it's not just a matter of it being harder to see; the visual cues are different. Instead of the bright redness typically seen in lighter skin, you'll often notice a more diffuse, darker red or reddish-brown discoloration. This is because melanin in darker skin can mask the true extent of erythema, making it harder to diagnose.",
